---
/**
 * InnerBoard OS (the ios view of the client's design): the people operating system for organizations, the IOS
 * workflow, the Company OS Score, and the book behind it. The Company OS Score form opens an email to the team
 * with what was entered (the site has no form backend).
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Practice.astro";
import AppPhone from "../components/AppPhone.astro";

---
<Layout title="InnerBoard OS · The Practice" description="You’ve built the business. Now build the people who can grow it. InnerBoard IOS develops the confidence, capability, and ownership of the people you already pay." path="/ios" nav="ios">
<section class="view ios-page" id="ios">
  <div class="phero">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div class="stack">
        <svg class="inq-mark os-mark" viewBox="0 0 200 200" role="img" aria-label="InnerBoard OS logo"><circle cx="100" cy="100" r="96" fill="#1B2332"/><path d="M72.6 175.2 A80 80 0 1 1 178.8 86.1" fill="none" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/><defs><path id="osArc" d="M86.3 177.8 A79 79 0 0 0 177.3 83.6"/></defs><text font-family="Instrument Sans,Helvetica Neue,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="12.5" letter-spacing="4.6" fill="#B08D57"><textPath href="#osArc" startOffset="2%">INNERBOARD</textPath></text><text x="100" y="124" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fraunces,Georgia,serif" font-weight="300" font-size="74" letter-spacing="-1" fill="#F3EDE5">OS</text></svg>
        <p class="eyebrow">InnerBoard OS · IOS</p>
        <h1>You’ve built the business. Now build the people who can grow it.</h1>
        <p class="sub-ios">You can build a team that leads itself. It just takes practice.</p>
        <p class="sub-ios">Your business has an operating system. Your people need one too.</p>
        <p class="lede">InnerBoard IOS helps you accelerate the value of the people you already pay by developing the confidence, capability, and ownership to do their best work.</p>
        <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#ios-contact">Get Your Company OS Score <span class="arr">→</span></a><a class="btn btn-line" href="#ios-contact">Talk to Our Team</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ph photo hero-gfx"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="563" src="/images/practice/ios-team.webp" alt="A leadership team in conversation around a conference table"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band tight">
    <div class="wrap features three" style="margin-top:0">
      <div class="feature"><h4>Stronger leaders</h4><p>At each level, not only the top.</p></div>
      <div class="feature"><h4>Accountable teams</h4><p>People who own their results without being chased.</p></div>
      <div class="feature"><h4>Measurable outcomes</h4><p>Progress you can see and track.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Most performance problems are people problems.</h2>
      <div class="problems">
        <div><h4>Leaders are stretched thin.</h4><p>Owners and managers carry decisions their teams could own.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Accountability is inconsistent.</h4><p>Expectations live in people’s heads, so follow through varies.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Execution is inconsistent.</h4><p>The same work gets done well one week and missed the next.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Your people aren’t keeping pace with growth.</h4><p>The business is moving faster than their judgment and ownership.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Good people leave.</h4><p>Turnover is expensive, and it tends to start with culture.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Change doesn’t stick.</h4><p>Trainings feel good for a week, then old habits return.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band">
    <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">The cost</p>
        <h2>The cost doesn’t always show up as a line item.</h2>
        <p class="lede">It shows up in the work that stalls when one person isn’t in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="costs">
        <li>Decisions that never get made</li>
        <li>Problems that keep coming back</li>
        <li>Opportunities that get missed</li>
        <li>Leaders stuck following up</li>
        <li>A founder who stays essential to most decisions</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="opportunity">The opportunity isn’t simply to get more from your people. It’s to develop more of what they’re capable of bringing to the business.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band blue on-navy">
    <div class="wrap model">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 400 400" role="img" aria-label="The IOS model: Leadership, Culture, Behavior, Results, and Valuation around IOS at the center">
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="188" fill="none" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".35" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        <g fill="none" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".75" stroke-width="1.4">
          <circle cx="200" cy="105" r="72"/>
          <circle cx="290.3" cy="170.6" r="72"/>
          <circle cx="255.8" cy="276.9" r="72"/>
          <circle cx="144.2" cy="276.9" r="72"/>
          <circle cx="109.7" cy="170.6" r="72"/>
        </g>
        <path d="M60 110 A170 170 0 0 1 112 52" fill="none" stroke="#CBB089" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <path d="M106 50 L114 51 L110 58" fill="none" stroke="#CBB089" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        <circle cx="200" cy="200" r="38" fill="#4A6A9A" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".6"/>
        <text x="200" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fraunces,Georgia,serif" font-size="28" fill="#F3EDE5">IOS</text>
        <g font-family="Instrument Sans,sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.8" fill="#F3EDE5" text-anchor="middle">
          <text x="200" y="84">LEADERSHIP</text>
          <text x="318" y="168">CULTURE</text>
          <text x="276" y="304">BEHAVIOR</text>
          <text x="124" y="304">RESULTS</text>
          <text x="82" y="168">VALUATION</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The solution</p>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:12px">A people operating system for high performing organizations.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:14px">IOS works alongside the systems, training, and leadership development you already have. It focuses on how your people operate, not only on what the business requires of them.</p>
        <p class="chain">Leadership → Culture → Behavior → Results → Valuation</p>
        <dl class="defs">
          <div><dt>Leadership</dt><dd>How people lead themselves and influence others.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Culture</dt><dd>The environment, expectations, and experiences that shape how people show up.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Behavior</dt><dd>The daily choices, actions, and habits that determine execution.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Results</dt><dd>The performance created through consistent behavior and shared accountability.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Valuation</dt><dd>The value created by stronger people, more reliable execution, and less dependence on any one person.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band" id="ios-process">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The IOS workflow</p>
      <h2 class="h2">How IOS works.</h2>

      <div class="assess">
        <div class="stack">
          <span class="stepnum">1</span>
          <h3>Assess</h3>
          <p class="lede">Start with the Company OS Score. It shows your team’s strengths, development needs, role expectations, and what’s influencing performance right now. This becomes your baseline.</p>
          <a class="textlink" href="#ios-contact">Get your Company OS Score →</a>
        </div>
        <AppPhone screen="company-os-score" width={290} alt="The Company OS Score in The Practice app: 64 out of 100, in transition, with the three lowest areas and the chapters that fix them." />
      </div>

      <ol class="steps" start="2">
        <li><b>2</b><h4>Develop</h4><p>Build the self leadership skills and capacity your business needs through The Track: Personal Power and Social Influence.</p></li>
        <li><b>3</b><h4>Apply</h4><p>Turn learning into daily behavior with a Role Blueprint that defines what each role is paid to produce.</p></li>
        <li><b>4</b><h4>Practice</h4><p>Each person gets a seat in The Practice app and practices the behaviors daily, on the job.</p></li>
        <li><b>5</b><h4>Measure</h4><p>Track module completion and progress. Individual answers stay private. Leaders see progress in counts.</p></li>
        <li><b>6</b><h4>Certify</h4><p>Train internal leaders through INQ (for working with clients) or OS Certification (for working with a team or organization).</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band blue on-navy">
    <div class="wrap cycle-wrap">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">One connected system</p>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:0">Continuous development, not a one time training.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Each step feeds the next. What you measure shapes what your people develop next, and certified leaders keep it running inside your business.</p>
        <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#ios-contact">Get Your Company OS Score <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
      <svg class="cycle" viewBox="0 0 420 420" role="img" aria-label="Cycle: Assess, Develop, Apply, Practice, Measure, Certify, then back to Assess">
        <defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="6" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10z" fill="#CBB089"/></marker></defs>
        <circle cx="210" cy="210" r="150" fill="none" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".25" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="3 6"/>
        <g fill="none" stroke="#CBB089" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#ah)">
          <path d="M254 66 A150 150 0 0 1 320 104"/>
          <path d="M358 186 A150 150 0 0 1 358 234"/>
          <path d="M320 316 A150 150 0 0 1 254 354"/>
          <path d="M166 354 A150 150 0 0 1 100 316"/>
          <path d="M62 234 A150 150 0 0 1 62 186"/>
          <path d="M100 104 A150 150 0 0 1 166 66"/>
        </g>
        <g font-family="Instrument Sans,sans-serif" font-size="12.5" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.4" text-anchor="middle">
          <g><circle cx="210" cy="60" r="44" fill="#F3EDE5"/><text x="210" y="56" fill="#B08D57" font-size="11">01</text><text x="210" y="73" fill="#1B2332">ASSESS</text></g>
          <g><circle cx="340" cy="135" r="44" fill="#2E4C78" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".5"/><text x="340" y="131" fill="#CBB089" font-size="11">02</text><text x="340" y="148" fill="#F3EDE5">DEVELOP</text></g>
          <g><circle cx="340" cy="285" r="44" fill="#2E4C78" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".5"/><text x="340" y="281" fill="#CBB089" font-size="11">03</text><text x="340" y="298" fill="#F3EDE5">APPLY</text></g>
          <g><circle cx="210" cy="360" r="44" fill="#2E4C78" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".5"/><text x="210" y="356" fill="#CBB089" font-size="11">04</text><text x="210" y="373" fill="#F3EDE5">PRACTICE</text></g>
          <g><circle cx="80" cy="285" r="44" fill="#2E4C78" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".5"/><text x="80" y="281" fill="#CBB089" font-size="11">05</text><text x="80" y="298" fill="#F3EDE5">MEASURE</text></g>
          <g><circle cx="80" cy="135" r="44" fill="#2E4C78" stroke="#F3EDE5" stroke-opacity=".5"/><text x="80" y="131" fill="#CBB089" font-size="11">06</text><text x="80" y="148" fill="#F3EDE5">CERTIFY</text></g>
        </g>
        <text x="210" y="204" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fraunces,Georgia,serif" font-size="34" fill="#F3EDE5">IOS</text>
        <text x="210" y="228" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Instrument Sans,sans-serif" font-size="10.5" letter-spacing="2" fill="#B4B8C2">ONE CONNECTED SYSTEM</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The outcome</p>
      <h2 class="h2">What changes when your people have an operating system.</h2>
      <div class="outcomes">
        <div>More ownership</div><div>Stronger execution</div><div>Greater leadership capacity</div>
        <div>Less founder dependency</div><div>A stronger culture</div><div>Greater enterprise value</div>
      </div>
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:56px">Who it’s for</p>
      <div class="audience"><span>Founders and owners</span><span>CEOs and executive teams</span><span>Growing organizations</span><span>Organizations preparing for their next stage</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band" id="ios-contact">
    <div class="wrap split" style="align-items:start">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">Get started</p>
        <h2>Get your Company OS Score.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Tell us a little about your organization. We’ll start with your baseline and walk you through the IOS workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <form class="form" id="iosForm">
        <label for="f-name">Name<input id="f-name" required autocomplete="name"></label>
        <label for="f-org">Organization<input id="f-org" required autocomplete="organization"></label>
        <label for="f-email">Work email<input id="f-email" type="email" required autocomplete="email"></label>
        <label for="f-size">Team size<select id="f-size"><option>Under 25</option><option>25 to 100</option><option>100 to 500</option><option>500 plus</option></select></label>
        <label class="full" for="f-goal">What would you like to improve?<textarea id="f-goal"></textarea></label>
        <div class="full ctas"><button class="btn btn-solid" type="submit">Get Your Company OS Score <span class="arr">→</span></button></div>
        <p class="msg" id="iosMsg" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="band navy on-navy">
    <div class="wrap book">
      <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1000" height="1499" class="book-cover" src="/images/practice/replaceable-cover.webp" alt="Book cover: IrReplaceable, The Internal Operating System, by Leah Roling, afterword by Tim O’Donnell">
      <div class="stack">
        <p class="eyebrow">The thinking behind IOS</p>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:0"><em>Replaceable</em>, by Leah Roling.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Why your people are capable of more than their job description, and how to build it into the way your business runs.</p>
        <div class="ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="#ios-contact">Talk to Our Team <span class="arr">→</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>
